WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.120
We enjoyed sports.

2
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:08.980
I mean football and . . . like I said, I watched LSU since I was a boy.

3
00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:15.660
I think our great players in those days was like . . . Well, Steve Van Buren became one of the finest players.

4
00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:20.360
Alvin Dark and Sulcer Harris, a local boy, were great tailbacks.

5
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.440
Who else?

6
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.416
Well, Abe Mickal.

7
00:00:24.416 --> 00:00:26.900
Abe Mickal and Jess Fatheree,

8
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:37.940
that’s all that bunch came up in the thirties but . . . I was a kid watching Jess Fatheree run 102 yards on a football fake punt behind the goal line,

9
00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:42.560
took off for 102 yards on the football field.

10
00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:46.547
And Abe Mickal was one of the top players they, you know, they had.

11
00:00:46.547 --> 00:00:52.667
Old Huey [Long], he pulled the strings of the football players and the coaches . . . And the band.

12
00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:57.480
Oh, Castro [Carazo] and the band, was million dollar band.

13
00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:02.200
Anybody make that trip to Austin when we played at Texas University in Austin?

14
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:10.528
They put out tracks and the train coaches from here on a flatbed barge and took us across to Brusly [Louisiana].

15
00:01:10.528 --> 00:01:12.060
It is on Brusly’s side.

16
00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:15.260
We all went on the trip to University of Texas.

17
00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.460
They took the whole band.

18
00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.440
It was quite a . . . quite a thing.

19
00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.840
It was just like when they went to the [1944] Orange Bowl [played in Miami, Florida, against Texas A&amp;M].

20
00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:29.380
I think they had a . . . Where was I reading where Lewis Gottlieb [City National Bank president and University supporter] leased so many cars and got some gas cans?

21
00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:35.340
Football team, they had to go by train because they didn’t have any gas, or any way to get them down there.

22
00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.280
But, they still went down there to the Orange Bowl.
